  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reduce the burden of TB in Tanzania</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Holistic approach to reduce the burden of tuberculosis in Tanzania, collaborating with 3 different partners, including a patient organisation with  national coverage. The program outcome is that the rights and needs of people affected by TB are met. KIDH works mainly with drug resistant TB. The project focusses on the rights and needs of men, women and children affected by TB through a gender sensitive and rights based approach. TB and gender analysis are undertaken and actions adjusted according. Other partners of LHLI in Tanzania are: Temeke Municipality and KIDH (Kibongoto Infectious Disease Hospital).</narrative>
  </description>
